    "narrative": "The **Zurich Zebras** project a high-upside slate for 2026-08-07, anchored by the elite 73.39 score of **Yordan Alvarez**. Despite facing a same-handed matchup against Robbie Ray, **Alvarez** maintains an elite xwOBA of .473, and his massive base projection overrides the minor platoon penalty. We are also heavily leaning into the speed-driven upside of **Christian Yelich** (69.09) and **Kyle Schwarber** (65.24). **Yelich** benefits significantly from the slow delivery of Zebby Matthews, which provides a high-probability environment for stolen bases\u2014our most critical scarcity category\u2014while **Schwarber** receives a substantial boost from his lead-off role, despite the 33% rain risk in his contest against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. **Colt Keith** (64.14) rounds out the top tier of starters, as his favorable park factors and the exploitable xERA of JT Brubaker provide a clear path to production.\n\nRegarding bench composition, the decision to leave **Carson Benge** (54.65) on the pine was the most difficult pivot. **Benge** scored marginally higher than **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (55.02), yet **Crow-Armstrong** remains in the utility slot to capitalize on his lead-off volume, which the optimizer consistently prioritizes over **Benge**\u2019s mid-order projection. While **Hector Rodriguez** possesses an elite .578 xwOBA, his score of 47.22 is suppressed by the difficult matchup against Cade Cavalli, forcing him to the bench alongside **Chase Meidroth** and **Josh Smith**. We must maintain vigilance regarding the 33% rain risk affecting **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber**; if these games are delayed, the lack of late-game pivots\u2014given that **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** are not currently optimized for action\u2014could constrain our daily efficiency. We proceed with our primary lineup, betting that the high-speed profiles of **Trea Turner** and **Christian Yelich** mitigate the risks posed by today's rotation.",
